FIND(1)                     User Commands                    FIND(1)

NAME
    find - recursively search a directory hierarchy

SYNOPSIS
    find [path...] [expression]

DESCRIPTION
    find visits each starting path and its descendants. With no path it starts
    at the current directory. All supplied tests must match.

EXPRESSIONS
    -name pattern       match the final path component using *, ?, and []
    -type f | -type d   select regular files or directories
    -mindepth number    suppress entries above the given depth
    -maxdepth number    do not descend below the given depth
    -print              print each matching path followed by a newline
    -print0             print each matching path followed by a NUL byte
    -exec command {} ;  execute command once for each match, replacing every
                        {} occurrence with the path

EXAMPLES
    find /etc -type f -name '*.conf'
    find . -print0 | xargs -0 wc -l

SEE ALSO
    xargs(1)
